@baseUrl = http://localhost:8055
@token = oOBvq33MC5K3nGRAmCGVrfHHh8n5F3ep
@testPageId = REPLACE_WITH_CREATED_PAGE_ID

### 1) Health check (no auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/server/health

### 2) Who is this token?
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me?fields=id,email,role,policies,status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3) Effective permissions (best overview)
GET {{baseUrl}}/permissions/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4) Check effective pages permissions only
GET {{baseUrl}}/permissions/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5) Raw permission rows for pages/page_blocks
GET {{baseUrl}}/permissions?fields=id,collection,action,permissions,validation,presets,fields&filter[collection][_in]=pages,page_blocks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6) Raw permission rows for block collections used by pages
GET {{baseUrl}}/permissions?fields=id,collection,action,permissions,validation,presets,fields&filter[collection][_in]=block_hero,block_richtext,block_form,block_posts,block_gallery,block_pricing,page_blocks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7) Can this token read pages?
GET {{baseUrl}}/items/pages?limit=1&fields=id,title,permalink
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8) Optional write test (creates one draft page)
# Run only if you want to verify create permission explicitly.
POST {{baseUrl}}/items/pages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"title": "Permission Test",
	"permalink": "/permission-test",
	"status": "draft"
}

### 9) Cleanup optional write test
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/items/pages/{{testPageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

